{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1526763657,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MDQzMjM3NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2510#issuecomment-390432374"},"message":"\u003e The comments already hint towards a --list-commands\n\nYeah, each time I've looked at that I've thought, \"meh, not really a priority because you can easily inspect things with git log --grep=RUNCMD, etc\".  But ...\n\n\u003e [...] it would be useful to be able to programatically inspect run records\n\nin that case, yeah, that seems more useful.  I haven't  given much thought to what information the results dict should actually include, though.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1526799830,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MDQ2MjI3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2510#issuecomment-390462272"},"message":"Brain dump:\n\nAt the very minimum the entire run record, of course. In addition to that:\n- `commit`: the shasum of the commit\n- `timestamp`: of the commit\n- `author`: of the commit\n- `path`: dataset path","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1526921192,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MDcxMjM3MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2510#issuecomment-390712370"},"message":"Would would be really help full is an included changeset in the style of `datalad diff` (across repository boundaries). \n\nWhen using this to record updates in some kind of meaningful directory structure quite informative logs or visualizations can be built based on the corresponding JSON output.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527086800,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTM3NDY5MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2510#issuecomment-391374690"},"message":"Annnd, if we can get structured data out, it would be super-useful to amend the run record with additional structured data!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1527087089,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTM3NjQ3NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2510#issuecomment-391376475"},"message":"\u003e Annnd, if we can get structured data out, it would be super-useful to amend the run record with additional structured data!\n\nSorry, I'm not following.  Can you give me an example?\n\n(I'm working on this now, btw.)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527088935,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTM4ODA3Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2510#issuecomment-391388077"},"message":"So, let's say I build this fancy pipeline system that knows a bit more why what kind of command was executed. It would want to record this information in the changeset somehow. E.g. 'results recomputed due to bug in software used for commit X.\n\nWe would not want to blow up the run record with all of that arbitrary info, but we also would not put it in the commit message as an unstructured English blurb.\n\nA minimalistic solution would be if a system using `run` could say \"add this one key/value combo to the run record\".   It would then be able to point to a file that is produced as an output and recorded in the dataset. This file could have any format and size and only needs to be understood by said system. As a consequence, this system could use `rerun --dry-run` or better `rerun --report` to rediscoved the knowledge it deposited and build fancy stuff on top of it.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1527089862,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTM5MzgwNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2510#issuecomment-391393805"},"message":"OK, I think I've got it.\n\n\u003e using run could say \"add this one key/value combo to the run record\". It would then be able to point to a file that is produced as an output and recorded in the dataset. \n\nRight, I think that'd be useful.  (The same idea has come up in conversations with @yarikoptic.)\n\n\u003e As a consequence, this system could use rerun --dry-run or better rerun --report to rediscoved the knowledge it deposited and build fancy stuff on top of it.\n\nOK, so there's nothing special for `rerun --dry-run` to do then because it will already include the run info dict.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527090881,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTM5OTgxMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2510#issuecomment-391399812"},"message":"\u003eThe same idea has come up in conversations with @yarikoptic\n\nThat is the thing with the Russians and the Germans -- you can't tell them apart ...\n\n\u003e rerun --dry-run\n\nWhat do you think about `--report` instead?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1527092476,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTQwOTI1Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2510#issuecomment-391409257"},"message":"\u003e What do you think about --report instead?\n\nI think `--report` is a better name in terms of capturing the possible uses.  When I see `--dry-run`, I just think \"run this first to make sure I don't screw anything up\".","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1527094270,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTQyMDY4NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2510#issuecomment-391420685"},"message":"Hmm, just tried to switch things over from `--dry-run` to `--report`, but the cli 